+# TASK-260830-3uessl review verdict
+
+## Verdict
+
+**Changes requested -> `to-dev`.** CR `CR-TASK-260830-3uessl-1` revision 1 is
+not accepted.
+
+Review target: base `8441818417458d7e88a46470e40ee376d99eea26`, candidate
+tree `777c2fabe2214a64f05311593c3fd11f0bfc8053`. Every changed working-tree
+blob matches the candidate tree, and the attached CR patch matches the exact
+binary diff (see `candidate-integrity-02.log`).
+
+## Blocking findings
+
+### F1. Published durable-operation evidence is not the exact pinned contract
+
+`internal/catalog/catalog.go:75-86` promises that durable operations carry an
+**exact** idempotency scope and recovery evidence, and README makes the same
+claim. The generated Terminal Backend rows do not meet it:
+
+- `internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json:18` cites `7.1.4-7.1.5`, which does not
+  exist anywhere in the pinned source tree. Appendix D binds the Terminal
+  Backend protocol fixtures to Sections 4.B-4.C; capabilities are in Section
+  4.D.
+- Lines 24-26 encode create as `(create, bootstrap_operation_id)`. Pinned
+  Section 4.C defines `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` and the canonical
+  UTF-8 key `session_id + "/" + bootstrap_operation_id`.
+- Lines 29-31 encode attach as `(attach, terminal_instance_id, client_id)`.
+  Section 4.C defines `terminal_instance_id + "/" + client_id`.
+- Lines 34-36 collapse quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,
+  terminate-stale, and restore into `(operation, operation_id)`. Section 4.C
+  gives distinct canonical keys based respectively on quiescence generation,
+  provider proof kind, safe-boundary evidence, stale lease/epoch, and
+  session/bootstrap operation.
+- `TB-CREATE-IDEMPOTENCY` and `TB-ATTACH-IDEMPOTENCY` are absent from the entire
+  pinned specification tree, so they cannot serve as the claimed fixture
+  evidence.
+
+The exact source used for this comparison is
+`relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`;
+its `SPEC.md` SHA-256 is
+`562546d240f0fa3e71b47e6359a002f9892c0efd97e19eb55917527552ac484a`, matching
+the implementation lock. Evidence is in `reviewer-normative-comparison-01.log`.
+
+Impact: consumers of the typed catalog receive incorrect recovery keys and
+nonexistent traceability while the API and README describe those facts as
+exact. This fails the crash/idempotency and specification-traceability portions
+of the acceptance criteria.
+
+Required rework: correct and regenerate the Terminal Backend rows, splitting
+operations whose canonical keys/recovery rules differ. Audit every durable
+operation family against the pinned source rather than assuming a non-empty
+string is evidence. Use actual section anchors and pinned fixture IDs/anchors.
+
+### F2. The negative gate proves deletion only and accepts narrowed or forged facts
+
+`internal/cataloggen/generate.go:271-278` validates only that the idempotency
+string and recovery list are non-empty. `TestGenerateRejectsNarrowedDurableMutationEvidence`
+at `internal/cataloggen/generate_test.go:127-138` deletes the recovery list
+entirely; it does not narrow the gate. `internal/catalog/catalog_test.go:189-202`
+likewise checks only presence, not exact values. Normative sections and fixture
+families are also accepted as arbitrary non-empty strings.
+
+Reviewer probes drove the real generator CLI and demonstrated both surviving
+negative shapes:
+
+- a non-empty but narrowed `bootstrap_operation_id` key with one invented
+  `retry somehow` evidence string was accepted and emitted;
+- `section-does-not-exist` plus `fixture-does-not-exist` was accepted and
+  emitted.
+
+See `reviewer-narrowing-probe-01.log` and
+`reviewer-traceability-probe-01.log`.
+
+Impact: the green suite does not fail when the exact durable-operation or
+traceability contract is narrowed. This violates the required negative-evidence
+shape and leaves the same class of defect as F1 undetectable.
+
+Required rework: add exact positive fixtures for every generated field that
+claims normative semantics, and a true narrowing mutant that keeps fields
+present while changing/removing part of their required scope. Bind section and
+fixture references to a closed reviewed source (or assert the complete reviewed
+metadata projection exactly) so invented non-empty values cannot pass.
